---
/**
 * who-its-for.astro — the full differentiation argument (D-264).
 *
 * What it is: the case the home page only gestures at, given room. It names
 * DaVinci Resolve and Premiere Pro directly, describes accurately what they ask
 * of a user, and says what Apelles assumes instead — then says out loud who it
 * is NOT for, which is the part that makes the rest believable.
 * What it does NOT do: claim to beat a professional NLE at professional
 * editing, or soften the comparison into "easier to use". Every right-hand
 * column below is a shipped capability with a real MCP tool behind it, checked
 * against mcp/server.py by tests/mcp-data.test.ts.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Signature from '../components/Signature.astro';
import { CONTRASTS, LIMITS } from '../data/product.ts';
---

<Base
  title="Who Apelles is for — made for people who never learned to edit"
  description="DaVinci Resolve and Premiere Pro were built by editors, for editors who already have the craft. Apelles assumes the opposite: that you know what you want and not how to build it, and that building it is the machine's job."
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="Who it’s for"
    title="You don’t need to know how to edit."
    lede="Apelles is for the person who has something worth showing and no idea which button starts a cut. That is not a stripped-down version of a professional tool. It is a different assumption about who is sitting there."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell two">
      <h2>The assumption every editing app makes about you.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Open Premiere Pro for the first time and it hands you a timeline, a program monitor, an
          effect controls panel and several hundred keyboard shortcuts. Open DaVinci Resolve and
          you get a whole page of node graphs. None of this is badly designed &mdash; it is some of
          the best-designed software there is. All of it is designed for somebody who already knows
          what a J-cut is, why you would ripple rather than roll, and what a vectorscope is telling
          them.
        </p>
        <p>
          That person exists and is very well served. If you are not that person, the tool does not
          meet you halfway. It waits. Most people give up in the waiting, and the video they had in
          their head never gets made.
        </p>
        <p>
          Apelles starts from the other end. You describe the result you want in ordinary words, and
          an agent does the technical execution &mdash; the cutting, the colour, the motion graphics
          &mdash; through the real controls, in front of you, on the same undo stack you use. The
          craft is still happening. It is just not being asked of you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>The same job, both ways.</h2>
      <p class="lede intro">
        Neither column is a caricature. The left is genuinely what the work involves when you do it
        by hand. The right is a shipped capability, and the name underneath it is a function an
        agent can call today.
      </p>

      <ol class="jobs">
        {
          CONTRASTS.map((c) => (
            <li class="job">
              <p class="want">{c.want}</p>
              <div class="ways">
                <div class="way">
                  <p class="tag">By hand, in a professional NLE</p>
                  <p>{c.craft}</p>
                </div>
                <div class="way here">
                  <p class="tag">In Apelles</p>
                  <p>{c.here}</p>
                  <p class="tool mono">{c.tool}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell two">
      <h2>Who this is not for.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          If you edit for a living, Resolve is faster than this and will stay faster for a long
          time. You already have the craft, and describing an edit in a sentence is mostly overhead
          when you could simply perform it. We are not going to pretend a working editor is who
          this was built for.
        </p>
        <p>
          You are welcome here anyway &mdash; the colour work is real, the timeline is a real
          multi-track NLE, and handing the tedious passes to an agent is genuinely useful at any
          skill level. But the person we are building for is the one who has never opened an NLE
          and is not planning to learn one.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>And what it is not, yet.</h2>
      <ul class="limits">
        {LIMITS.map((l) => <li>{l}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section close">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">If that sounds like you</p>
      <p class="ask">
        There is no build to download yet. There is a list, and one email when there is something
        worth installing.
      </p>
      <Signature href="/#beta" label="Request beta access" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    max-width: 18ch;
    font-weight: 300;
  }

  .two {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 1rem + 5vw, 5.5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .prose p {
    max-width: 60ch;
    color: var(--pigment-basalt-soft);
  }
  .prose p + p {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .band {
    background: var(--pigment-marble-deep);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--edge);
  }

  .band h2 {
    max-width: 24ch;
  }

  .intro {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
  }

  /* ---- the two-ways list ---------------------------------------------- */

  .jobs {
    list-style: none;
    margin: clamp(2rem, 1.25rem + 2.5vw, 3rem) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .job {
    padding-block: clamp(1.5rem, 1rem + 1.5vw, 2.25rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--edge);
  }
  .job:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--edge);
  }

  /* What the person actually wants, in their own voice. The serif italic is the
     only place on this page the display face raises its voice. */
  .want {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.3;
    max-width: 30ch;
  }

  .ways {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.25rem, 0.75rem + 2vw, 3rem);
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }

  .way p:not(.tag):not(.tool) {
    color: var(--pigment-basalt-soft);
    max-width: 44ch;
  }

  .tag {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--pigment-basalt-soft);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  /* The right-hand column gets the working colour on its label and a hairline
     down its edge — enough to say "this side" without a box or a checkmark. */
  .here {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--pigment-terracotta);
    padding-left: clamp(0.9rem, 0.6rem + 0.6vw, 1.25rem);
  }
  .here .tag {
    color: var(--pigment-terracotta);
  }

  .tool {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    color: var(--pigment-basalt-soft);
  }

  /* ---- limits ---------------------------------------------------------- */

  .limits {
    list-style: none;
    margin: clamp(1.75rem, 1.25rem + 1.5vw, 2.5rem) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.1rem;
    max-width: 76ch;
  }

  .limits li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.25rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--pigment-basalt-soft);
  }
  .limits li::before {
    content: '';
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 1px;
    background: var(--pigment-ochre);
    margin-top: 0.62em;
  }

  /* ---- close ----------------------------------------------------------- */

  .ask {
    margin: 1rem 0 2rem;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    line-height: 1.35;
    max-width: 30ch;
  }

  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .two {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    h2 {
      max-width: 24ch;
    }
    .ways {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
